# =============================================================== ETIOLOGY OF THE SECOND PROCESS
V(T_MIX, IO_D,
  "A 66-year-old man with lactic acidosis from postoperative sepsis receives an opioid by a pump and is now drowsy with shallow breathing. " + ABG("7.15", "36", "12") + "; " + NACL(137, 101) + ". Which part of his history best explains his concurrent respiratory acidosis?",
  [["The opioid pain medicine",
    "Correct. Expected carbon dioxide = 1.5 x 12 + 8 = 26, range 24 to 28; his 36 is above it, a concurrent respiratory acidosis. Respiratory depressants such as narcotics cause decreased ventilation, matching his drowsiness and shallow breathing."],
   ["The postoperative sepsis",
    "Sepsis explains his raised-gap lactic acidosis (gap 137 - (101 + 12) = 24), and in sepsis the breathing is usually driven up, toward respiratory alkalosis. Tell: the respiratory acidosis needs a cause of decreased ventilation, here the opioid.", "adjacent fact"],
   ["Anxiety after surgery",
    "Anxiety causes hyperventilation and a respiratory alkalosis, lowering carbon dioxide. His 36 is above the predicted 24 to 28. Tell: anxiety would push carbon dioxide below the Winter range, not above it.", "reversed direction or value"],
   ["Saline given in surgery",
    "Saline infusion causes a normal-gap metabolic acidosis, which lowers bicarbonate; it does not raise carbon dioxide. His second process is respiratory. Tell: a carbon dioxide above the Winter range needs a cause of underbreathing.", "confused mechanism or drug class"]],
  CS(49, 32, 36), "etiology", "etiology"),

V(T_MIX, IO_D,
  "A 58-year-old woman on dialysis for kidney failure missed a week of sessions, has vomited for 4 days and feels anxious. " + ABG("7.40", "38", "23") + "; " + NACL(137, 93) + ". " + DELTA + "which part of her history best explains the metabolic alkalosis?",
  [["Her vomiting",
    "Correct. Gap = 137 - (93 + 23) = 21, change in gap = 11, but change in bicarbonate = 25 - 23 = 2: a metabolic alkalosis is holding the bicarbonate up. Vomiting loses gastric hydrochloric acid, a saline-responsive cause, and her low chloride fits."],
   ["Her kidney failure",
    "Kidney failure with uremia explains the raised gap of 21, the metabolic acidosis half of this pair. Tell: the alkalosis needs a cause that adds bicarbonate or removes acid, and vomiting removes gastric acid.", "adjacent fact"],
   ["Diarrhea from her illness",
    "Diarrhea loses bicarbonate and gives a normal-gap acidosis with a high chloride; her chloride is 93, low. Tell: lower gastrointestinal losses drop bicarbonate; upper losses from vomiting raise it.", "reversed direction or value"],
   ["Her anxiety",
    "Anxiety causes hyperventilation and a respiratory alkalosis, which lowers carbon dioxide; it does not raise bicarbonate, and her carbon dioxide of 38 is near normal. Tell: a change in gap larger than the change in bicarbonate needs a metabolic, alkalinizing cause such as vomiting.", "confused mechanism or drug class"]],
  CS(30, 50, 53), "etiology", "etiology"),

